  "description": "AWUMUE crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group I 41/a. Reported CIF formula moiety: C44 H68 Er6 N16 O33 4+,4(C11 H7 N4 O2 1-). From the CIF bond table, Er1 (Er) has 9 O neighbors; Er2 (Er) has 9 O neighbors; Er3 (Er) has 9 O neighbors; Er4 (Er) has 9 O neighbors; Er5 (Er) has 9 O neighbors; Er6 (Er) has 9 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 15 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.674-5.423 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.73-180.00°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Er6(μ6-O)(μ3-OH)8(L2)4(H2O)16]. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ6-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 16 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
